# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# SOUL — a trippy ROYGBIV liquid marble you can roll around an infinite plane.
#   • the marble's skin is a live water/oil liquid sim in rainbow (ROYGBIV) mode
#   • a rapidly colour-cycling vector ring overlay glows on top (additive — the
#     liquid shows underneath)
#   • it HUMS: a ling-audio tone whose pitch follows the colour cycle and whose
#     volume rises with motion + squash
#   • WASD rolls it, SPACE jumps + double-jumps; it deforms (soft body) and
#     bounces off the ground with springy restitution
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

bind start = do {
    open_window(1920, 1080)
    set_ambient(0.2)
    set_zdist(32.0)
    audio_volume(0.5)

    bind R = 2.0
    bind GROUND = 3.0                       # +y is down, so the floor is below
    bind ball = soft_ball(0.0, 0.0 - 2.0, 0.0, R)
    soft_kick(ball, 0.4, 0.0, 0.3, 0.06)

    # the marble's liquid skin (ROYGBIV)
    bind liq = liquid_new(56.0, 56.0)
    liquid_rainbow(liq, 1.0)
    bind sx = 0.0
    while sx < 56.0 {
        liquid_splat(liq, sx, 18.0, 1.0, 0.9, 2.2)   # oil band
        liquid_splat(liq, sx, 38.0, 0.0, 1.0, 2.4)   # water band
        bind sx = sx + 3.0
    }

    bind jumps = 0.0
    bind wasSpace = 0.0
    bind px = 0.0  bind py = 0.0  bind pz = 0.0     # previous centroid (for speed)

    while window_is_open() {
        bind t = time_now()

        # ── input: WASD roll (translate + spin so it tumbles & deforms), SPACE
        # jump/double-jump. Roll axis = up × move_dir (screen-down up = −y), and
        # the spin rate ≈ surface_speed / R so it rolls without obviously slipping.
        if key_down("a") { soft_kick(ball, 0.0-1.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.018)  soft_spin(ball, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0-1.0, 0.12) }
        if key_down("d") { soft_kick(ball, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.018)      soft_spin(ball, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0, 0.12) }
        if key_down("w") { soft_kick(ball, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0-1.0, 0.018)  soft_spin(ball, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.12) }
        if key_down("s") { soft_kick(ball, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0, 0.018)      soft_spin(ball, 0.0-1.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.12) }
        bind sp = 0.0-1.0
        if key_down("space") { bind sp = 0.5 }
        if sp > 0.5 { if wasSpace < 0.5 { if jumps < 2.0 { soft_kick(ball, 0.0, 0.0-1.0, 0.0, 0.750)  bind jumps = jumps + 1.0 } } }
        bind wasSpace = sp

        # ── physics: gravity, ground bounce (springy, deforms on impact) ──
        soft_step(ball, 0.016, 12.0)
        soft_bounce(ball, GROUND, 0.72)

        bind c = soft_centroid(ball)
        bind cx = c[0.0]  bind cy = c[1.0]  bind cz = c[2.0]
        # grounded? reset the jump counter when resting on the floor
        if cy + R > GROUND - 0.25 { bind jumps = 0.0 }
        # motion (for the hum + a *gentle, bounded* slosh — big values drain the
        # grid and the marble goes black, so we clamp the coupling hard)
        bind vx = cx - px  bind vy = cy - py  bind vz = cz - pz
        bind speed = sqrt(vx*vx + vy*vy + vz*vz)
        bind gxs = sin(t * 0.7) * 18.0
        if vx >  0.04 { bind gxs = gxs + 16.0 }
        if vx < 0.0-0.04 { bind gxs = gxs - 16.0 }
        bind gys = 24.0
        if vy < 0.0-0.04 { bind gys = 12.0 }       # a little buoyant lift on impact
        liquid_gravity(liq, gxs, gys)
        liquid_step(liq, 0.016)
        # keep the marble alive: top up two drifting blobs every frame so the
        # fluid never decays below the visible threshold (lava-lamp persistence)
        liquid_splat(liq, 28.0 + sin(t * 1.3) * 15.0, 20.0 + cos(t * 1.1) * 9.0, 1.0, 0.22, 3.0)
        liquid_splat(liq, 28.0 + cos(t * 0.9) * 15.0, 36.0 + sin(t * 1.7) * 9.0, 0.0, 0.24, 3.2)
        bind def = soft_deform(ball)

        # ── the HUM: the ball SINGS its own physics ──────────────────────────
        #  • pitch  ← height off the ground (higher = higher) + a bit of linear speed
        #  • volume ← linear speed + angular spin + squash on impact
        #  • timbre ← angular velocity drives the 4-D cross-modulator (faster spin →
        #             richer, beating, hyperdimensional tone)
        #  • filter ← the oil/water MIX opens a master low-pass: when the two fluids
        #             are separated it sounds dark/muffled; as they churn together it
        #             brightens and shimmers (the rainbow liquid as an audio filter)
        bind ang = soft_angular_speed(ball)               # tumbling/rolling rate
        bind height = GROUND - cy                         # 0 at floor, grows when airborne
        if height < 0.0 { bind height = 0.0 }
        bind mix = liquid_mix(liq)                         # 0 separated .. 1 churned
        # base pitch from height + linear speed; overall loudness from motion+squash
        bind base = 120.0 + height * 55.0 + speed * 180.0
        bind amp = 0.04 + speed * 4.0 + ang * 0.5 + def * 0.35
        if amp > 0.5 { bind amp = 0.5 }
        bind wdim = 1.0 + ang * 8.0                        # 4-D beating grows with spin
        # ── a 5-voice additive synth; the spectral balance follows the physics ──
        #   the harmonics swell with spin, the fifth blooms as the fluids mix,
        #   a detuned voice shimmers with speed, and a sub-octave gives it body.
        audio_tone(0.0, 0.0, cy, 0.0, wdim, base,        amp * 0.85,                 4.0 + ang*5.0, 0.03 + def*0.06)
        audio_tone(1.0, 0.0, cy, 0.0, 1.0,  base * 2.0,  amp * (0.22 + ang * 1.1),   3.0, 0.02)
        audio_tone(2.0, 0.0, cy, 0.0, 1.0,  base * 1.5,  amp * (0.16 + mix * 0.5),   2.0, 0.015)
        audio_tone(3.0, 0.0, cy, 0.0, 0.0,  base * 0.5,  amp * 0.55,                 1.0, 0.01)
        audio_tone(4.0, 0.0, cy, 0.0, 2.0,  base * 2.01, amp * (0.10 + speed * 0.6), 6.0 + ang*4.0, 0.05)
        audio_fx_lowpass(0.18 + mix * 0.8)                 # mixing opens the master filter
        audio_listener(1.0, 0.0, cos(0.2), sin(0.2))

        # ── render: ground grid (scrolls with the marble), then marble, then overlay ──
        set_color(6, 6, 14)
        fill()
        set_camera(1.0, 0.0, cos(0.2), sin(0.2))
        set_ambient(0.4)
        set_blend(1)

        # infinite ground: a grid centred under the marble (world offset by -cx,-cz)
        set_color(40, 55, 95)
        bind offx = cx - floor(cx / 2.0) * 2.0
        bind offz = cz - floor(cz / 2.0) * 2.0
        bind g = 0.0 - 12.0
        while g <= 12.0 {
            draw_line_3d(g - offx, GROUND, 0.0-12.0 - offz,  g - offx, GROUND, 12.0 - offz)
            draw_line_3d(0.0-12.0 - offx, GROUND, g - offz,  12.0 - offx, GROUND, g - offz)
            bind g = g + 2.0
        }
        flush_3d()

        # the marble: liquid sphere drawn at the ball's height, centred (camera follows x/z)
        liquid_draw_surface(liq, 1.0, 0.0, cy, 0.0, R * (1.0 + def*0.4), R)

        # ── motes suspended *inside* the orb, filling its volume (snow-globe) ──
        # they tumble as a cloud + wobble individually, depth-shaded so the orb has
        # real interior volume. Tint shifts slowly through the spectrum.
        bind pr = (sin(t*0.5)*0.5+0.5)*120.0 + 135.0
        bind pg = (sin(t*0.5+2.094)*0.5+0.5)*120.0 + 135.0
        bind pb = (sin(t*0.5+4.188)*0.5+0.5)*120.0 + 135.0
        orb_particles(0.0, cy, 0.0, R * 0.92, 240.0, t, pr, pg, pb)
        flush_3d()

        # ── outer shell: ONE trippy grayscale vector pattern wound around the orb.
        # It's a guilloché weave of spirals whose brightness fades with depth
        # (front bright, back dark) → a translucent grayscale "texture" with alpha,
        # not a cage. It rolls with the ball (rot_y over time, rot_x tilts with vx)
        # while the ROYGBIV liquid marble glows through underneath.
        #orb_shell(0.0, cy, 0.0, R * 1.16, t * 0.9, t * 0.35 + vx * 5.0, 11.0, 232.0, 232.0, 238.0)
        flush_3d()

        # ── a few twinkles around the soul ──
        bind sc = project_3d(0.0, cy, 0.0)
        if sc[0.0] > 0.0 - 90000.0 {
            bind ssx = sc[0.0]  bind ssy = sc[1.0]  bind depth = sc[2.0]
            bind rpx = R * 520.0 / depth
            if rpx > 600.0 { bind rpx = 600.0 }
            if rpx < 8.0 { bind rpx = 8.0 }
            sparkle(ssx - rpx, ssy - rpx, rpx*2.0, rpx*2.0, 28.0, t)
        }

        bind px = cx  bind py = cy  bind pz = cz
        set_blend(0)
        present()
    }
}
